    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Shimmer Myr before playing a land drop this turn. The player has Plains, Island, and Port Town in hand but hasn't played a land yet. Playing a land first is almost always correct - it preserves information and flexibility. Additionally, Shimmer Myr gives flash to artifacts, meaning it could have been cast at end of an opponent's turn instead, keeping mana open and hiding information. Playing a land first (like Port Town, revealing a Plains/Island to have it enter untapped) would give access to more mana this turn.",
